  Barrier condition:
  max_{v in \partial_C b(z)} v . f(z,u,d) + alpha(b(z)) >= 0
  for all d in D.
```

**Explanation.** Because the signed distance is locally Lipschitz but not everywhere differentiable, the barrier condition uses Clarke's generalized gradient and Filippov solutions. This ensures the condition is well-defined at corners and non-smooth points of the boundary.

